117
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:10,100
So let's get started, shall we?

118
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:14,700
Scoutmaster ship in seven minutes or less.

119
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,700
Scouts forget a lot of things.

120
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:27,700
They forget their water bottle,

121
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:29,700
They forget their sleeping pad,

122
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:31,700
They forget food.

123
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:33,599
They forget a lot of things when they go camping,

124
00:06:33,599 --> 00:06:38,800
and they usually forget to do one pretty important thing,

125
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,599
And that is to say thank you.

126
00:06:40,599 --> 00:06:42,800
Now we're not doing what we do as Scouters

127
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:45,099
So that Scouts will come up to us and say thank you

128
00:06:45,099 --> 00:06:48,800
or shower us with gifts or praise or anything like that.

129
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:51,500
I mean, if we were doing it because of that,

130
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:54,099
most of us would be probably be pretty disappointed

131
00:06:54,099 --> 00:06:55,700
in the result.

132
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:59,099
But Scouts do say thank you in a lots of ways

133
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:01,500
that you just have to listen for because-

134
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:04,200
because it's rarely going to be coming straight up to you

135
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:06,800
with a hearty handshake and a pad on the back.

136
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:09,300
Now, most of the time, it's just in the way

137
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,800
that they live their lives

138
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:14,000
and in the effect that your work has on them.

139
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,200
Now, Baden Powell said that Scouts should not expect

140
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:19,100
life to be a bed of roses,

141
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:22,500
and he said that there probably would be no fun in it

142
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,700
if it was.

143
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:26,700
We're all going to come up against discouragement

144
00:07:26,700 --> 00:07:30,400
and we're all going to have setbacks and disappointments,

145
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:33,099
But facing down the difficulties

146
00:07:33,099 --> 00:07:36,099
is where we really end up finding the greatest satisfaction,

147
00:07:36,099 --> 00:07:36,800
isn't it?

148
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:39,800
It's usually where we accomplish the greatest work

149
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,500
and make the most difference

150
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,800
When nothing seems to be working,

151
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,800
when nothing comes out as you planned.

152
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,400
take heart,

153
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,500
I mean, you have no idea

154
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,400
what your work as a Scouter will do

155
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,900
in the lives of the Scouts you serve.

156
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:55,000
Now here's where I'd like to tell you some

157
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,200
inspirational story about overcoming adversity,

158
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,900
or how a stone dropped in a pond makes ripples,

159
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:01,800
or something like that.

160
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:03,200
But I'm not going to do that

161
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,900
because you've heard all those stories already.

162
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:07,900
The message is simple:

163
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:09,200
You matter

164
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,400
and the work that you're doing matters.

165
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:14,000
Now. you may influence the course of history,

166
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,100
or you may just make your little corner of the world

167
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:18,900
a bit brighter,

168
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,300
But the scale of the results

169
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,900
does not affect the importance

170
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,600
of who you are

171
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,000
and what you do.

172
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,400
So I'm going to encourage you to work hard,

173
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,500
Give a little more,

174
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,000
go a little further.

175
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,400
It may be that that next half-step

176
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,800
is what really matters,

177
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:38,100
what really brings success.

178
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:41,000
I'm going to tell you not to expect anything,

179
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,900
but to expect everything.

180
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:45,000
If we tie the work that we do as Scouts

181
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,200
to rewards,

182
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,200
we're going to be discouraged

183
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:50,000
if they don't show up.

184
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,300
Do the work

185
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:53,300
because it's the right thing to do.

186
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:54,800
That's reason enough

187
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,900
And you will be rewarded.

188
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:58,500
You will be rewarded

189
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:01,500
because you've made the world a better place.

190
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:02,900
Your rewards aren't coming to you

191
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:04,199
wrapped in fancy paper

192
00:09:04,199 --> 00:09:05,599
and tied with a bow.

193
00:09:05,599 --> 00:09:06,900
They may not be coming to you

194
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,599
in a frameable certificate

195
00:09:08,599 --> 00:09:09,800
to put up on your wall

196
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,599
and another patch,

197
00:09:11,599 --> 00:09:12,800
But they're there.

198
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,300
Do good work,

199
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,400
Be nice,

200
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,699
Be faithful,

201
00:09:16,699 --> 00:09:17,900
Be honest,

202
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,400
Reach deep down

203
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,400
and find the compassion

204
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:23,300
and the understanding and love

205
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:24,500
you know is there,

206
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,400
and keep going on.

207
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,900
When the choice is between

208
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:30,000
being angry or helpful,

209
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,100
choose helpful.

210
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:32,500
When the choice is between

211
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:33,600
being judgmental

212
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:35,500
or being understanding,

213
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:37,199
be understanding

214
00:09:37,199 --> 00:09:38,600
Above all,

215
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,000
catch the spirit of scouting,

216
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,300
and that spirit is simple:

217
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:42,600
It's the love

218
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,600
of our fellow human beings

219
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,300
and the natural world

220
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:48,199
and the author of it all.

221
00:09:48,199 --> 00:09:49,800
Some people call that author God,

222
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,900
Some people call it by other names.

223
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:54,000
There's one important thing.

224
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,200
It's tapping into that source of power

225
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,200
and love and compassion

226
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:00,700
is how we best serve our scouts

227
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:02,000
and each other.

228
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,300
We do good work as scouters.

229
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,600
We make a difference.

230
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,000
Never doubt it

231
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,600
and thank you for doing it.

232
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:22,700
Good that you do.

233
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:25,100
Welcome back to you,

234
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:33,100
It don't cost very much.

235
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:35,800
Find me a letter,

236
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:39,100
Send it by name

237
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,500
Email. that is folks.

238
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:44,600
And here's an answer to one of your emails.

239
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,800
Ladies and gentlemen,

240
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,800
the story you are about to hear is true,

241
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:56,800
Only the names have been changed

242
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,800
to protect the innocent.

243
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:06,800
That's right.

244
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,800
We're withholding the name

245
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,800
on this particular email

246
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,800
to protect the innocent.

247
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:12,800
Anyway,

248
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:14,800
I'm going to give you an answer

249
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:16,800
to this particular email.

250
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,800
I'm going to give you an answer

251
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,800
anyway.

252
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:20,800
The author said:

253
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:22,800
I've been a new scout master for less than a year

254
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:24,800
and the troop I took over is a great one,

255
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,800
with almost 25 years

256
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,800
and several dozen Eagles in their history.

257
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,800
A scout brought to my attention

258
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,800
that our troop policy on boards of review

259
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,800
may need to be adjusted.

260
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,800
Our process is that

261
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,800
once I've had a scout master conference

262
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:39,800
and signed the scouts book.

263
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:41,800
I notify the committee that the scouts

264
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:43,800
eligible for a border review

265
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,800
and then we ask the boy

266
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:47,800
to do one of two things.

267
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:49,800
one: tender foot to second class,

268
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,800
He has to contact the advancement chair

269
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:53,800
so a board of review

270
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,800
can be scheduled.

271
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,800
If he's from first class to life,

272
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,800
he needs to contact three adults

273
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,800
off a list that is provided

274
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:03,800
out of 16, plus parents

275
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:05,800
that are trained in conducting boards of review,

276
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,800
to schedule the meeting.

277
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,800
Our thought that this is a good practice for a scout

278
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,800
and it provides needed experience

279
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,800
interacting with adults and scheduling.

280
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,800
It also follows our idea

281
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,800
of not doing what a scout should do.

282
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,800
This has been a practice in the troop going back

283
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,800
probably about 15 years

284
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,800
and three different scout masters.

285
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,800
I've been catching up with all your podcasts

286
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,800
and I'm almost listening to them all.

287
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:29,800
I recall one podcast where this was discussed

288
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,800
and that others handle

289
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,800
setting up boards of review in a similar fashion.

290
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:35,800
So now I have a scout

291
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:37,800
ready for his first class

292
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:39,800
board of review and he sent me an email

293
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,800
quoting from the 2013

294
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,800
guide to advancement.

295
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,800
the scout master does not have the authority

296
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,800
to expect a scout to request

297
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,800
or organize a board of review,

298
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:51,800
and that a scout has no

299
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,800
part in selecting any board of review members.

300
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,800
I've learned a lot from you, Clark,

301
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:57,800
and I'm looking for some guidance.

302
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:59,800
How does your troop handle scheduling

303
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:01,800
boards of review? What we do is

304
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:03,800
we have a board of review scheduled once a month.

305
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,800
That's the troop meeting

306
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,800
directly after our monthly

307
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:09,800
camp out. That's dedicated

308
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,800
to the patrol leaders council

309
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,800
meeting and a board of review

310
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:15,800
and scout master conferences.

311
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:17,800
It's kind of an administrative night.

312
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,800
I've been encouraging our advancement committee

313
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,800
not only to have boards of review

314
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,800
for scouts who are advancing

315
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,800
but to invite scouts who are not advancing

316
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,800
so they have a board of review

317
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,800
at least twice a year.

318
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,800
Now this hasn't quite caught on yet,

319
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,800
but I'm told they're working on it.

320
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:35,800
All we need to know from a scout

321
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:37,800
is that he will be attending

322
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:39,800
and you know what. sometimes they show up,

323
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,800
but I typically conduct a scout master conference

324
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,800
directly before

325
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,800
they go to a board of review.

326
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,800
I think you've got an excellent theory.

327
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,800
Scouts should learn to schedule things

328
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,800
and put themselves forward. So why do you think

329
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,800
that the BSA policy

330
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,800
is actually

331
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:57,800
180 degrees from this good

332
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:59,800
idea that you have?

333
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,800
Now, I'm not implying any ill will

334
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,800
or bad intentions on your part

335
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,800
or on the part of anyone involved.

336
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,800
I'm sharing my own experience

337
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,800
and my evolution on the subject.

338
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:11,800
I'm not saying that what you are doing

339
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,800
doesn't work or it's misapplied

340
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:15,800
or that it's a particularly bad idea,

341
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,800
but it's

342
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:19,800
obviously outside the policy.

343
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,800
There's a pretty slight adjustment on your part

344
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,800
to fix it, and I've made

345
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:25,800
many such adjustments over the years.

346
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,800
What I thought was a good idea

347
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,800
wasn't, and I worked to understand

348
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,800
and align things with the policy,

349
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:33,800
Not because I was fearful of reprisals

350
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:35,800
if I didn't, but because I wanted

351
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,800
to understand why the policy was

352
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:39,800
the way it was.

353
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,800
Perhaps you'd agree with me that the problem

354
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,800
with the idea of making Scouts responsible

355
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,800
for scheduling a border review

356
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,800
is because the border review

357
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,800
is not really their responsibility.

358
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:51,800
It's a responsibility

359
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:53,800
of the advancement committee.

360
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,800
I'm not saying that your troop does,

361
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,800
but it's not hard to imagine

362
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:59,800
how requiring Scouts to initiate

363
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:01,800
a border review request

364
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,800
could be misapplied

365
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:05,800
or a stumbling block,

366
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:07,800
and this is sadly true in some unit.

367
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:09,800
If you read section 8

368
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:11,800
of the Guide to Advancement 2013-

